---
import LandingLayout from '@/layouts/LandingLayout.astro';
import { rentalTerms } from '@/data/rental-terms';
import { neighborhoodFor } from '@/data/neighborhood-content';

const { deposit, mileage, cancellation } = rentalTerms;
const local = neighborhoodFor('south-beach');

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Do you bring cars to beachfront hotels?',
    a: 'We deliver throughout South Beach, hotels included. Give us the property and the date when you get in touch and we will agree the handover point in advance, so nobody is circling the block trying to find each other on the day.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How far ahead should I book for a big event week?',
    a: `As early as you can settle your dates. Art Basel, the Grand Prix, Ultra, the Boat Show and spring break all compress supply across the city at once, and a six-car fleet has no slack in it. ${cancellation.summary}`,
  },
  {
    q: 'What does the daily rate cover?',
    a: `${mileage.includedPerDay} miles for every day booked, counted as one pooled allowance across the rental instead of resetting each morning. A refundable ${deposit.display} deposit is held against the car and released once it has been checked over on return.`,
  },
];

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: f.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a } })),
};
---
<LandingLayout
  title="Exotic Car Rental South Beach | Lussaro Collection"
  description="Rent exotic cars in South Beach with Lussaro Collection. Premium supercars and luxury vehicles delivered along Ocean Drive and Collins Avenue."
  h1="Exotic Car Rental South Beach"
  intro="Our delivery area covers South Beach — the beachfront hotels, the blocks off Ocean Drive and Collins Avenue, and the streets either side of Lincoln Road."
  ctaTitle="Reserve your South Beach exotic"
  schema={[faqSchema]}
>
  <h2>Delivered to the beach side</h2>
  <p>South Beach is flat and mostly horizontal: hotel forecourts, kerbside valet stands and surface lots rather than the stacked garages found inland. Lincoln Road is a pedestrian mall, so any handover happens on the cross streets. Tell us where you are staying and the car is brought over.</p>
  {local?.deliveryLogistics && <p>{local.deliveryLogistics}</p>}

  <h2>Choosing a car for South Beach</h2>
  <p>The good news for anyone eyeing a supercar: the barrier that makes low cars awkward elsewhere — steep ramps down into a building — is largely absent here. Handovers happen at ground level, which suits the <a href="/cars/huracan-evo">Huracan EVO</a> and the <a href="/cars/sf90">Ferrari SF90</a> far better than a tower garage would. Both still sit low at the nose, so the usual caution applies at any raised kerb or driveway lip.</p>
  <p>What South Beach substitutes instead is congestion and tight kerbside space. Ocean Drive moves slowly by design, and hotel forecourts on the older blocks were not laid out for a car nearly seven feet wide. That is worth weighing if you are drawn to the <a href="/cars/rolls-royce-cullinan">Cullinan</a> or the <a href="/cars/mercedes-maybach-gls-600">Maybach GLS 600</a>, both of which are large enough to need a moment's thought at a busy forecourt. The <a href="/cars/mercedes-s580">S580</a> threads through it all with the least fuss.</p>

  <h2>Booking around the calendar</h2>
  <p>A handful of weeks tighten availability across Miami, not just the beach. Art Basel lands in early December, the Grand Prix in May, Ultra in March, the Boat Show in February, and spring break runs from late February into April. With six cars, those dates go first — if your trip overlaps one, fix the dates early.</p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  {faqs.map((f) => (
    <>
      <h3>{f.q}</h3>
      <p>{f.a}</p>
    </>
  ))}
  <p>Staying downtown instead? See <a href="/exotic-car-rental-brickell">Brickell</a>, or the full picture on our <a href="/exotic-car-rental-miami">Miami page</a>.</p>
</LandingLayout>
